# TradingAgents Security

Read `docs/ops/security-development.md` for credentials, private data, external
content, API/web/database work, deployment, or future broker integration.

## Mandatory Rules

- Never commit or print secrets or populated environment files.
- Treat portfolio/account data as private financial data.
- Keep server credentials out of client/frontend code.
- Treat external text and model output as untrusted.
- Allowlist tools and validate arguments, symbols, URLs, and paths.
- Do not disable TLS verification.
- Validate structured output; free text cannot authorize a sensitive action.
- Logs/analytics must omit raw credentials, account identifiers, private
  portfolio details, and unrestricted model/vendor payloads.

## Platform Rules

Private web/API data requires authentication and owner authorization. Long jobs
use durable workers. Public deployment requires rate limits, audit logs,
backups, recovery, monitoring, and a threat-model review.

## Broker Rule

No broker write credential or order path may be introduced without a separately
approved paper/live security and risk contract.
